.TH DNSSEC-SIGN 1 "2026-08-18" "rgbdns 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dnssec-sign \- sign tinydns source as an offline DNSSEC snapshot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dnssec-sign
.RI [ data
.RI [ data.signed ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads one disposition line per authoritative zone from
.I dnssec
in the working directory. A K line signs its zone and a Uzone line explicitly
preserves an unsigned zone. The command atomically writes tinydns text, adds
DNSKEY, NSEC, and RRSIG records, and rejects unmaterialized ANAME, conditional
or expiring records that cannot be represented by this diagnostic text export,
pre-existing signing data, and policy/zone mismatch. Use dnssec-data to retain
qualified records in U zones directly in CDB form.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, 100 for usage errors, and 111 for operational failures.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dnssec-data (1),
.BR dnssec-check (1),
.BR aname-materialize (1)
